WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome to ear biscuits,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.330
the podcast where two lifelong
friends talk about life

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:09.850
for a long time.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.210
I'm Link.
And I'm Rhett,

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.970
this week at the round
table of dem lighting,

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:17.680
we're going to be sharing
our recent family adventures

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.430
that happened to each of us
over the Thanksgiving break.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.910
Aha, I went to Disneyland.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:24.950
I didn't.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.310
So I got some fresh observations,

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.160
cause it's been a while since
I've been there my friend,

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.170
Well, you've been at Disneyland

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:37.360
at least three times more than I have.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.000
That's my daughter's--
Since the last time I went--

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.480
She's a Disney freak.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.030
I haven't been to
Disneyland in four years,

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:44.140
five years, probably.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.085
How's your back?

00:00:46.085 --> 00:00:46.918
Horrible
I could tell

00:00:46.918 --> 00:00:50.370
when you walked in that
there was something going on.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.230
Well, one of the things
that we'll talk about

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:56.460
is we actually spent
Thanksgiving day together.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.810
Did you notice that my back

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.277
was pretty messed up on Thanksgiving day?

00:01:00.277 --> 00:01:01.760
No.
I didn't...

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.770
So it was messed up the whole week--

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.674
You just seem so grateful,
that's all I noticed.

00:01:05.674 --> 00:01:10.674
And it was starting to
get better by Thursday.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:16.060
And then yesterday, we're
recording this on a Monday,

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.063
yesterday, Sunday after Thanksgiving.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.280
I'm like, "I'm back"

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.480
What?
I'm back.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.942
And I'm like, "My back is back."

00:01:23.942 --> 00:01:24.790
Okay.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.010
No more pain.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:27.320
Do you know what triggered it?

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.120
I think I do, and then last night,

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.380
I'll tell you what I
think it triggered it.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.213
It was back,

00:01:31.213 --> 00:01:32.350
the back pain was back,

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.640
Yeah, but then last...

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:34.620
So I go to bed.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.460
I'm like, "You got a big week."

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.803
We're doing some things that
we can't talk about yet.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.213
And I tend to, whenever there's a--

00:01:41.213 --> 00:01:43.240
When talk about it? Dammit.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.950
The fact that it frustrates you so much

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.928
is I find very interesting. What--

00:01:46.928 --> 00:01:48.750
Because it's the main thing on my mind.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.480
Yeah, but I like keeping secrets.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.060
I don't like not talking about things

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.570
that are on my mind.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:55.403
Okay.

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.290
Whenever we're getting--
Especially when it's good.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:01.350
Whenever we're getting
ready to do something new,

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:04.152
I've noticed a pattern that
my back will go out like,

00:02:04.152 --> 00:02:05.878
"I'm getting ready to travel,

00:02:05.878 --> 00:02:07.260
"and we're getting ready
to do this new thing."

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.060
So I've developed this ability

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.720
to just associate this stress or whatever

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.080
does something in the back muscles.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:14.913
I don't know how it works.

00:02:14.913 --> 00:02:15.746
Tension.

00:02:15.746 --> 00:02:17.210
But what that has done for me

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:20.330
is it has let me not get too
stressed out when it happens.

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:22.100
So it's like, "Okay, this is temporary."

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.360
This isn't like--
Oh,

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.620
Gonna be around for months
and months and months.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.280
It used to be around for a long time--

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.000
So you're stressed out, which causes it,

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.850
but you're not getting stressed out

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.470
about the back problems

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.910
because that would make it even worse,

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:35.220
and that's what's happened in the past.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.417
Because I'm usually able to be like,

00:02:36.417 --> 00:02:37.927
"Okay, you're gonna do your stretches.

00:02:37.927 --> 00:02:39.640
"There'll be a few days."

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.840
Sometimes it might just be a few hours.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.070
You never really know.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.510
This one lasted all week.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:45.910
And then, like I said, yesterday,

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:47.890
a full week later.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.860
Now the thing I did tie it to,

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.050
the physical thing I tied it to

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.980
is a really intensive
bench pressing session.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.403
Okay, now this might sound crazy to you.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:00.130
How does bench press--

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:00.963
So far yes.

00:03:00.963 --> 00:03:02.030
How does bench press--

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.020
Intense bench pressing.

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:04.530
Affect your lower back?

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:09.530
I was doing like an
especially long session

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.570
and it was really intense.

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:13.830
And then...

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:14.663
What's wrong with you?

00:03:14.663 --> 00:03:16.637
I'm just really showing
interest, go ahead.

00:03:16.637 --> 00:03:19.330
But see, this is the troubling thing

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.220
is I never really know

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.010
because I can always, almost always tie it

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.070
to either something that I did physically

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.470
or something that's stressing me out

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.260
because I'm always doing things physically

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.093
that might hurt me,

00:03:31.093 --> 00:03:33.410
and I'm always doing things in life

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:34.590
that might stress me out so--

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:35.423
Lifestyle man.

00:03:35.423 --> 00:03:36.730
And so I'm like, "How did--"

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:37.563
Cause the Sunday night

00:03:37.563 --> 00:03:39.950
after I did this bench pressing session,

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.687
I'm like, "Oh man, I'm really...

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:42.677
"Oh, this is a bad one.

00:03:42.677 --> 00:03:44.140
"This is a deep one."

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:45.860
I call it ground zero when it goes back

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.250
to what I feel is like
the original disc injury.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.190
Oh God.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:51.010
And, then I'm reading a book

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.350
that I got about back injuries.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.020
That's one of my pastimes.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.970
And--
Does that make it worse?

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.450
In the first three pages.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:02.500
The guy talks about avoiding bench press.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.690
I'm like, "What?"

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:07.432
And then he explains where
the pressure comes from.

00:04:07.432 --> 00:04:08.777
I'm like, "Well, must be
the bench press brother,

00:04:08.777 --> 00:04:11.760
"but it could be the fact that
I'm a little stressed out."

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.220
Long story short, he
suggested doing pushups

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:16.700
instead of bench press.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.350
Okay, so yesterday I'm better.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:22.460
I haven't worked out the
whole week cause of my back.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:24.840
So I'm like, "I'm gonna
do a hundred pushups.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:25.673
That's a lot.

00:04:25.673 --> 00:04:27.252
Not in one...

00:04:27.252 --> 00:04:29.023
I'll do like 20 sets of five.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.480
Okay, That works.
No, I do five set of 20.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.870
20 sets of five would be moronic.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.020
I do five sets of 20.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:35.880
No it wouldn't,

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.380
sometimes you gotta start with...

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.957
And after the...

00:04:39.957 --> 00:04:44.003
And so I did that and was fine,

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.690
all day yesterday.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:49.070
Last night while sleeping, which is,

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:50.233
this is so common,

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.970
while sleeping at like 2:00 AM,

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:56.017
I wake up and I'm like,

00:04:56.017 --> 00:04:58.117
"Uh-oh."

00:04:58.117 --> 00:04:59.107
It wasn't like I rolled over

00:04:59.107 --> 00:05:00.235
and it started hurting.

00:05:00.235 --> 00:05:01.340
It was just like I woke up

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:02.390
because it was hurting.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:03.223
Oh.

00:05:03.223 --> 00:05:05.310
And I was like, "Oh no, man."

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:06.143
I was like, "okay."

00:05:06.143 --> 00:05:08.220
And I tried to find a
comfortable position to sleep.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.053
Couldn't really.

00:05:09.053 --> 00:05:10.030
Did go back to sleep,

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:14.190
got up, did my like extra
long stretching routine

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.120
with the lacrosse ball

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.800
and all that stuff that I do every day.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.050
Okay.
Took some Advil,

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:22.770
put some Bengay on there and I'll be fine

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.200
Well that makes me giggle.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.880
I'll be fine. But I am glad.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.000
I'm glad that the thing that we're doing

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.140
that's stressing me out
is not happening today,

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:32.010
but happening tomorrow.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.410
And it does not involve bench press.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.550
Yeah, and it's not a physical thing.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.490
It's not like you have to be like...

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:40.080
Have a lot of lateral motion.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:42.200
As long as I can walk, and...

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.470
In fact, I did that this morning

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:44.303
as I walked through the kitchen,

00:05:44.303 --> 00:05:45.867
I was like, "Does it look
like something's wrong with me

00:05:45.867 --> 00:05:46.820
"when I walk?"

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:49.147
And she was like, "Hmm, only if you know

00:05:49.147 --> 00:05:50.530
"what you're looking for."

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:53.180
So when we talk about this
thing that we're gonna do,

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.960
that we finally get to talk about,

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.680
and we tell you the thing
that you can look for,

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.210
you'll know which one to look at

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.660
to then make a decision as to
whether or not you can tell

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:02.803
if my back was hurt.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.330
But I'm gonna be fine,
don't worry about me.

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:08.438
I'm in top physical form

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.900
Mentally

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:17.480
but physically, boy, lemme
just look at me, man.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.780
Good gracious.

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:21.080
Have you noticed how
I've been walking lately?

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:25.150
You'll be all right.
Just don't don't add--

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.130
The back panic.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.500
It's nice to know

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.070
that you've got that
you've got in his place.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.810
Because boy I remember the back panic

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:33.240
when you would just like...

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.723
You would be like, "Is this it?

00:06:36.557 --> 00:06:38.010
"Am I coming to see you Ethel?"

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:40.360
Or whatever Fred Sanford used to say.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:43.780
I'm not beyond traveling down to Panama

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:46.660
and getting some stem cells
injected in my lower back.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:47.980
Just so you know,

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:49.980
that is still a top of mine.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:52.370
Could that be monetized on YouTube?

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:53.980
Oh, hundred percent.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.710
It will be when we do it.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.110
Okay, great.
You should get some too.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:57.943
It's not gonna hurt you.
Oh yeah.

00:06:57.943 --> 00:06:58.930
I mean, I'll be there.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:00.500
I'll get some.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.610
I'll get some in the shoulder.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.100
That's why I don't bench press.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.800
Yeah, actually, you know what?

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:06.633
I'm gonna get some in my shoulder.

00:07:06.633 --> 00:07:08.590
My shoulder, it pops out

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:11.420
and then it will usually go right back in.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:13.620
And you can just get an
intravenously as well.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:16.290
You can just do a full treatment

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.400
and you feel like Superman.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.660
And you know what? Lily
has the same thing.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.460
Of course, to transition

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.663
into my vacation here.
Daughter's back.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:28.180
This is Lily's first
time back from college

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.400
for our Thanksgiving break,

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.720
so we we're looking forward to that.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.120
The whole reason that we
planned to go to Disneyland

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.050
was because she is obsessed with Disney.

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:38.083
She loves Disneyland.

00:07:39.233 --> 00:07:42.640
She's really into Marvel and Star Wars

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:45.960
and now that all that's folded
in to the park experience--

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:46.793
It's a smart move on their part.

00:07:46.793 --> 00:07:49.743
I do want to tell you about
the specifics of that.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:55.160
So we went for two days and the first...

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.273
We stayed in the hotel the first night.

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.340
We went to downtown Disney,

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:03.930
then bedded down for the night

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:06.630
for our first day at the
park, real fresh, real early.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.280
So we'd get an absolute full day.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.450
You stay in the park?

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.433
No, we stayed outside of the park

00:08:11.433 --> 00:08:13.470
in just like hotel.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.020
I was meaning like, wait till it closes

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:16.940
and like get under something.

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:18.030
No.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:20.220
there's an urban legend that
Lincoln was telling me about

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.810
that there's like that Mark Twain island

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:25.400
in the middle of Disneyland,

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.570
he said, some people swam over there

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.910
and stayed all night.
It's not an urban legend,

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:29.743
that's true.
And then they--

00:08:29.743 --> 00:08:30.576
Tom Sawyer Island.

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:32.830
Tom Sawyer, and then
they tried to swim back

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:37.420
with a baby and the
baby died or something.

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:38.470
I didn't listen too closely

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:42.920
because that was kind of
a downer early in the day.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:44.710
But, just so you know,

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:46.520
I'm not recommending it.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.070
You could easily stay inside there.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:51.220
There's so many places to hide.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:52.190
There's so many places to hide.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.720
Now if you get caught,
you're in a lot of trouble

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.663
and a whole family doing it,

00:08:55.663 --> 00:08:57.130
There's a lot at stake.

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:57.965
A family of five doing it?

00:08:57.965 --> 00:08:58.830
You know what I'm gonna do.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.320
I'm just gonna go sleep in a bed

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.537
and come back the next day,

00:09:01.537 --> 00:09:03.060
and just buy a second ticket.

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.090
Finding a comfortable
spot would be difficult.

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:06.430
But that next...

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:09.977
The first morning, Lily said,

00:09:09.977 --> 00:09:13.120
"I rolled over in my sleep
and my shoulder came out."

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:13.953
Oh man.
And I was like,

00:09:13.953 --> 00:09:15.980
"Did it go right back on her back in?"

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.580
No
Because they're back stuff.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.017
And I was like, "You know what?

00:09:19.017 --> 00:09:20.247
"I've given you this.

00:09:20.247 --> 00:09:21.377
"This is the genetic...

00:09:21.377 --> 00:09:24.217
"This is the physiology of
how your shoulders are built.

00:09:24.217 --> 00:09:26.150
"You're like me."

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:27.890
Sometimes I've rolled over in bed

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.163
or reach for something.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.130
I thought that I had
damaged it in middle school

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.070
when you started taking
me to that bench press,

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:39.550
behind the bathroom at the law school

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:43.030
that your dad gave us access to,

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:44.660
and we would go bench press there.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.340
And I would be pushing so much weight.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:49.850
And then I would start laughing and then--

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:51.873
We would have laugh attacks
about bench pressing.

00:09:51.873 --> 00:09:52.950
Then you would start laughing

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:54.650
and the bar would be on my chest.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:57.540
And you couldn't get it off of my chest.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:58.373
Cause I was laughing.

00:09:58.373 --> 00:09:59.690
Cause you were laughing so hard.

