00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:00.723
for having to...

00:20:00.723 --> 00:20:02.870
You have to clean up everything,
but you get more leftovers.

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:04.530
William brought the mac and cheese.

00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:05.870
And that mac and cheese was so good.

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:07.270
And there was so much of it.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:10.470
I had mac and cheese last night,

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:12.017
and I texted him about it and I was like,

00:20:12.017 --> 00:20:14.954
"Man, this is the gift
that keeps on giving."

00:20:14.954 --> 00:20:17.880
It's good for the immune
system too. Gunk it up.

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.393
I thought about that,

00:20:19.393 --> 00:20:22.003
and I think that on the whole,

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:23.870
I think the food I was eating

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:25.960
was better than other choices
I could have been making.

00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:27.460
I mean, turkey's good for you.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:29.970
There were some collards in there.

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:31.350
The sweet potatoes,
there's a lot of sugar,

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:32.730
but there's also a sweet potato.

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:34.396
That's good for ya.

00:20:34.396 --> 00:20:35.280
There was some collards.

00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:36.420
There's broccoli casserole,

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:37.365
which is still my favorite.

00:20:37.365 --> 00:20:38.907
Broccoli casserole--
It has broccoli in it.

00:20:38.907 --> 00:20:40.450
went real fast.

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:42.060
Actually, I was done with that on Friday.

00:20:42.060 --> 00:20:44.030
We had that for three
days. I was able to...

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:46.630
Cause I took it back.
I took most of it back.

00:20:46.630 --> 00:20:48.330
But man, it was so good.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:49.980
When you've got, listen--
Christy special,

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:51.280
Nothing against...

00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:53.880
You know, I already said
how much I love California.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.490
I love California.

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:57.170
But if you're from California

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:00.160
or you been here too long,

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:02.270
you've forgotten how to do Thanksgiving.

00:21:02.270 --> 00:21:03.103
I'm sorry.

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:06.380
Thanksgiving is not about being healthy.

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:07.967
It's about the food tasting good.

00:21:07.967 --> 00:21:09.490
I'm not going to tell the story again

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:10.944
about the super California Thanksgiving

00:21:10.944 --> 00:21:11.777
we went to that one time

00:21:11.777 --> 00:21:15.080
where they did deconstructed stuffing,

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:17.290
which made me wanted to
physically hurt the guy

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.780
who served it to me.

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:20.840
We had two types of stuffing.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.210
Oh wow, and they were both great.

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:24.000
One of them had meats in it.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:26.510
Well the one--
Sausages in the stuffing.

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:28.360
The ones that Jessie made is based on--

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:30.640
Or the dressing if you will.
Her mom's recipe

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:32.590
and it's got hot and sweet,

00:21:32.590 --> 00:21:35.690
like hot and maple sausage built into it.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:36.720
And it's big.

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:38.633
And then the one that Jenny made,

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:41.710
is the classic one that
like my momma makes,

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:44.070
which I actually prefer the classic one,

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:47.800
but I ate the hell out of both of them.

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:49.790
And so, anyway, I'm sorry.

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:51.230
Again, I love California,

00:21:51.230 --> 00:21:53.770
but it ruins your ability to
do Thanksgiving correctly.

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:56.270
You need to be from the south
and possibly the Midwest

00:21:56.270 --> 00:21:57.483
to get this correct.

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:01.560
This is the worst time to
be giving this feedback.

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:03.630
It's like, we need to
be given this feedback

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.053
right after Halloween.
Just replay this.

00:22:05.053 --> 00:22:08.280
But let me just talk quickly
about the turkey mishap

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:09.587
that I had because--

00:22:10.912 --> 00:22:13.140
I didn't discern one and I ate the turkey.

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:15.390
I embarrassed myself in
front of my neighbors.

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:16.300
Oh,

00:22:16.300 --> 00:22:18.253
At least I'm thinking I probably did.

00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:21.250
I'm a turkey guy.

00:22:21.250 --> 00:22:23.840
And I don't mean that by like
saying I really love turkey.

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:25.540
I'm saying that I'm the
guy that makes the turkey

00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:26.630
for Thanksgiving.

00:22:26.630 --> 00:22:27.470
Turkey's okay.

00:22:27.470 --> 00:22:28.990
Yeah.

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:31.470
I try to make it as good
as it possibly can be

00:22:31.470 --> 00:22:32.303
for the holiday.

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:35.180
I smoked one turkey

00:22:35.180 --> 00:22:37.580
and I don't mean like a
rolled it up in a joint.

00:22:39.310 --> 00:22:41.700
I put it on a grill

00:22:41.700 --> 00:22:44.540
I guess that is what some
people might think at first.

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:45.633
But I don't think that's what--

00:22:45.633 --> 00:22:46.770
Hey, it's California.

00:22:46.770 --> 00:22:49.360
I feel like in California Thanksgiving,

00:22:49.360 --> 00:22:50.193
you're smoking turkey.

00:22:50.193 --> 00:22:51.217
It's like, "What do you mean by that?

00:22:51.217 --> 00:22:52.416
"Is you're a pipe involved."

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:56.780
This means putting it on a grill,

00:22:56.780 --> 00:23:00.160
a smoker, it's smoking it for
an extended period of time.

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:03.190
I did a whiskey maple glaze on this thing.

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:06.720
I took the entire breastbone
of the turkey out,

00:23:06.720 --> 00:23:08.150
which is difficult
Beat that first,

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:09.084
that's always...

00:23:09.084 --> 00:23:09.917
Just get it out of the way
And so I could

00:23:09.917 --> 00:23:11.090
spatchcock the turkey,

00:23:11.090 --> 00:23:13.463
put it really flat, so it cooks evenly.

00:23:14.450 --> 00:23:15.610
It was great.

00:23:15.610 --> 00:23:17.570
Actually, I made a little mistake with

00:23:17.570 --> 00:23:18.750
it cooked faster than I wanted to,

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:20.420
I didn't get to crisp the
skin as much as I want it to

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:21.360
but set that aside.

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:24.366
I also deep fried two turkey breasts.

00:23:24.366 --> 00:23:25.199
Okay?

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:28.603
Jenny, who loves white meat.

00:23:30.580 --> 00:23:31.413
Our friend, Jenny,

00:23:31.413 --> 00:23:33.600
she brought these two turkey breasts

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:34.830
and she likes a fried turkey.

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:35.912
So I was like, "Yeah, I'll do it.

00:23:35.912 --> 00:23:37.237
"I'll get this electric fryer,

00:23:37.237 --> 00:23:39.000
"it makes it super easy."

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.450
So I pull this thing out.

00:23:40.450 --> 00:23:41.390
I've got the turkey...

00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:43.480
The smoking turkey is smoking.

00:23:43.480 --> 00:23:44.313
It's kinda doing its thing

00:23:44.313 --> 00:23:47.170
and I'm like, "Okay, I'm ready
to deep fry these turkeys."

00:23:47.170 --> 00:23:50.900
I got this electric smoker
that's like a big cube

00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:53.280
and I had three gallons of peanut oil

00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:54.920
that I was gonna use as my oil.

00:23:54.920 --> 00:23:56.640
You said smoker, but you meant fryer.

00:23:56.640 --> 00:23:57.473
Fryer. Sorry. Yeah.

00:23:57.473 --> 00:24:00.200
It's a fryer, electric fryer.

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:01.230
So it's not one of the ones

00:24:01.230 --> 00:24:02.680
where you put it over the open flame

00:24:02.680 --> 00:24:04.703
and you potentially burn your house down.

00:24:05.750 --> 00:24:07.530
Which I think I might
have to upgrade to that

00:24:07.530 --> 00:24:10.630
based on this story I'm
about to tell you though.

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:13.797
So I'm like, "Okay, I'm
gonna fill this thing up

00:24:13.797 --> 00:24:15.067
"with oil

00:24:15.067 --> 00:24:15.900
"and

00:24:17.287 --> 00:24:18.760
"turn it on."

00:24:18.760 --> 00:24:22.700
So as I'm getting ready to pour the oil,

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:25.270
the three gallons of oil into the fryer,

00:24:25.270 --> 00:24:26.737
I think to myself,

00:24:26.737 --> 00:24:29.277
"I remember there being
like a valve at the bottom

00:24:29.277 --> 00:24:32.260
"of this thing last year."

00:24:32.260 --> 00:24:34.720
It's like a valve that you
can open to drain the oil

00:24:34.720 --> 00:24:36.670
when you're cleaning it.

00:24:36.670 --> 00:24:39.930
But it's underneath this mechanism

00:24:39.930 --> 00:24:42.440
that's on the outside that
has the heating element,

00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:47.440
so I was like, "Surely I
didn't not close that valve.

00:24:47.787 --> 00:24:49.400
"What an idiot."

00:24:49.400 --> 00:24:50.850
And so I just pour it in there,

00:24:50.850 --> 00:24:53.950
and then I see that the
level's three gallons.

00:24:53.950 --> 00:24:56.190
I'm like, "See, I told
you I closed that valve."

00:24:56.190 --> 00:24:57.880
I turned around to do something,

00:24:57.880 --> 00:25:00.287
to mess with the other turkey.

00:25:00.287 --> 00:25:04.253
And I turn back around and
there is a pool of peanut oil

00:25:04.253 --> 00:25:06.360
that is spilling out all around the fryer,

00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:09.370
all on top of my outdoor bar area,

00:25:09.370 --> 00:25:10.517
Glug, glug, glug, glug,
glug, glug, glug, glug,

00:25:10.517 --> 00:25:12.200
Spilling down onto the concrete

00:25:12.200 --> 00:25:13.563
and going into the drain.

00:25:14.750 --> 00:25:15.583
Straight oil.

00:25:15.583 --> 00:25:16.700
Hey, good you got to drain.

00:25:16.700 --> 00:25:17.900
Straight to the ocean.

00:25:20.330 --> 00:25:22.423
So I panic,

00:25:23.730 --> 00:25:25.310
I pick up the heating element,

00:25:25.310 --> 00:25:28.630
which is attached to
the control mechanism,

00:25:28.630 --> 00:25:32.140
and I set the whole thing inside the oil.

00:25:32.140 --> 00:25:35.350
I didn't even remember doing
this until later when I looked

00:25:35.350 --> 00:25:37.833
and then I turned the
valve and I screw it up.

00:25:39.440 --> 00:25:40.273
And then--

00:25:40.273 --> 00:25:42.490
So you were able to find
the valve pretty quickly

00:25:42.490 --> 00:25:43.323
when you needed to.

00:25:43.323 --> 00:25:44.370
But yeah, but that was a lot of oil

00:25:44.370 --> 00:25:45.470
that had already left.

00:25:46.420 --> 00:25:48.040
And that was when I...

00:25:50.260 --> 00:25:53.450
Now I have neighbors,

00:25:53.450 --> 00:25:54.970
I have neighbors all around.

00:25:54.970 --> 00:25:56.420
And this is the--

00:25:56.420 --> 00:25:59.273
Do you have security cam
footage of this scramble?

00:26:01.420 --> 00:26:03.460
I don't have an angle on that part.

00:26:03.460 --> 00:26:04.333
I have an angle on the entrance.

00:26:04.333 --> 00:26:06.130
I'da think you'da had an angle

00:26:06.130 --> 00:26:07.530
on where you cook, so you
can see yourself cooking.

00:26:07.530 --> 00:26:09.480
You kinda know where my neighbors are.

00:26:09.480 --> 00:26:10.840
We share...

00:26:10.840 --> 00:26:12.680
The yards are all kind of together,

00:26:12.680 --> 00:26:13.513
but we kinda--
But they would have

00:26:13.513 --> 00:26:14.790
to all look down.

00:26:14.790 --> 00:26:15.850
They would look down on you.

00:26:15.850 --> 00:26:17.700
Oh, it's not about them seeing me,

00:26:17.700 --> 00:26:19.335
it's about them hearing me say,

00:26:19.335 --> 00:26:23.435
Oh

00:26:26.320 --> 00:26:27.153
just once?

00:26:27.153 --> 00:26:28.351
No, I said it a couple of times.

00:26:30.250 --> 00:26:31.890
I said it one time there,

00:26:31.890 --> 00:26:33.780
and then I went inside,

00:26:33.780 --> 00:26:34.613
told Jessie, I was like,

00:26:34.613 --> 00:26:38.299
"I made a big mistake and
give me some paper towels."

00:26:38.299 --> 00:26:39.132
And I was like,

00:26:39.132 --> 00:26:41.090
"Do you have..."
Cleaning up oil is tough.

00:26:41.090 --> 00:26:45.060
I said, "Do you have bath
towels that we don't need?"

00:26:45.060 --> 00:26:45.893
Hmm. Yeah.

00:26:45.893 --> 00:26:47.910
And she was like, "Yeah, these two."

00:26:47.910 --> 00:26:48.760
Two?
she had two

00:26:48.760 --> 00:26:51.090
that had like yellow stains on them.

00:26:51.090 --> 00:26:54.800
It's just from the wood from the sauna.

00:26:54.800 --> 00:26:56.240
So I'm like, "Okay."

00:26:56.240 --> 00:26:57.110
I go outside,

00:26:57.110 --> 00:26:59.340
and I start cleaning it up.

00:26:59.340 --> 00:27:01.230
And then I look and I realized,

00:27:01.230 --> 00:27:03.320
that's when I realized that
the whole heating element

00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:05.510
with the control mechanism

00:27:05.510 --> 00:27:07.300
Okay.
Is in the oil.

00:27:07.300 --> 00:27:08.600
Even the electronics.

00:27:08.600 --> 00:27:09.599
Like the dial,

00:27:09.599 --> 00:27:12.500
the electronic part of it.

00:27:12.500 --> 00:27:14.913
I pick it up
Oh you're having a--

00:27:17.310 --> 00:27:18.500
Louder this time.

00:27:18.500 --> 00:27:19.433
I'm sorry.

00:27:23.000 --> 00:27:24.680
And I was so mad.

00:27:24.680 --> 00:27:28.510
Like I get so mad at myself
when I make mistakes.

00:27:28.510 --> 00:27:30.210
It's not healthy, I'm in therapy.

00:27:30.210 --> 00:27:31.380
Is there any other word?

00:27:31.380 --> 00:27:35.530
I mean, you were over the edge.

00:27:35.530 --> 00:27:37.460
Yeah, and that was cause I held it up

00:27:37.460 --> 00:27:41.130
and saw the oil pouring out
of the inside of the housing.

00:27:41.130 --> 00:27:42.937
This is a fire hazard at this point.

00:27:42.937 --> 00:27:44.097
And so then I'm like,

00:27:44.097 --> 00:27:46.240
"I can't fry these turkeys,"

00:27:46.240 --> 00:27:47.150
because what are you gonna do?

00:27:47.150 --> 00:27:50.860
Plug in this fryer that's got
oil inside the electronics?

00:27:50.860 --> 00:27:51.827
No.
Well, that's what I did,

00:27:51.827 --> 00:27:55.140
and it worked fine

00:27:55.140 --> 00:27:58.060
Well, I let it drain
for a really long time.

00:27:58.060 --> 00:28:01.650
And then I was like, you have
to get oil very, very hot,

00:28:01.650 --> 00:28:03.500
Like think about the way
a heating element works.

00:28:03.500 --> 00:28:05.610
It's inside this thing,

00:28:05.610 --> 00:28:08.520
and it's designed to heat the
oil up to like 400 degrees.

00:28:08.520 --> 00:28:09.353
Yeah.

00:28:10.465 --> 00:28:11.540
The worst thing that could happen

00:28:11.540 --> 00:28:14.840
is the electric current,
which is what's happening

00:28:14.840 --> 00:28:16.560
in the heating element to hook it up,

00:28:16.560 --> 00:28:17.393
it's just gonna...

00:28:17.393 --> 00:28:18.700
It's not gonna catch it on fire.

00:28:18.700 --> 00:28:21.460
It's just gonna make it
hot inside the thing,

00:28:21.460 --> 00:28:24.380
and it'll probably smoke and
maybe melt some of the plastic,

00:28:24.380 --> 00:28:26.310
but I'll be able to tell.

00:28:26.310 --> 00:28:27.740
At least that was my theory.

00:28:27.740 --> 00:28:29.520
And I completely drained it,

00:28:29.520 --> 00:28:31.330
completely wiped it down,

00:28:31.330 --> 00:28:32.720
turned it on and watched it for 10 minutes

00:28:32.720 --> 00:28:34.580
before I proceeded and it was fine.

00:28:34.580 --> 00:28:36.290
Did you have the fire extinguisher ready?

00:28:36.290 --> 00:28:37.787
I brought the fire extinguisher out.

00:28:37.787 --> 00:28:38.667
Did you read it and say,

00:28:38.667 --> 00:28:41.710
"Is this an electrical fire
one or a grease fire one,"

00:28:41.710 --> 00:28:42.580
or "Oh, both."

00:28:42.580 --> 00:28:45.500
I looked at it and I
couldn't come to conclusions

00:28:45.500 --> 00:28:46.923
about that.
Yeah. You know.

00:28:46.923 --> 00:28:49.360
I just know I Wasn't
supposed to put water on it,

00:28:49.360 --> 00:28:50.280
but can you--

00:28:50.280 --> 00:28:52.440
The thing I feel about
fire extinguishers is this,

00:28:52.440 --> 00:28:55.840
if you got one that's that
is a victory and just use it,

00:28:55.840 --> 00:28:57.350
and see what happens.

00:28:57.350 --> 00:28:59.212
And you could say that you did your best.

00:28:59.212 --> 00:29:00.045
I don't...

00:29:00.045 --> 00:29:01.700
We need to look that up because--

00:29:01.700 --> 00:29:03.180
Yeah, we should
Is it bad

00:29:03.180 --> 00:29:06.000
to put a fire extinguisher
of any kind on a grease fire?

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:07.937
I know you can't put water on it but--

00:29:07.937 --> 00:29:09.960
#EarBiscuits, just let us know.

00:29:09.960 --> 00:29:11.490
But I will say

00:29:11.490 --> 00:29:15.190
that a couple of the
families that live around us,

00:29:15.190 --> 00:29:16.770
I believe our grandparents.

00:29:16.770 --> 00:29:19.450
Because during the holidays
you'll hear children.

00:29:19.450 --> 00:29:21.770
And during other times you
don't hear the children.

00:29:21.770 --> 00:29:22.990
It's either, they're a normal family

00:29:22.990 --> 00:29:25.610
that only lets kids
outside during holidays,

00:29:25.610 --> 00:29:26.950
which is possible.

00:29:26.950 --> 00:29:29.510
Or it's grandparents, you're
only having kids over.

00:29:29.510 --> 00:29:30.770
So they learned a word.

00:29:30.770 --> 00:29:32.180
And so I think that yeah,

00:29:32.180 --> 00:29:33.767
there were like,

00:29:33.767 --> 00:29:35.367
"That man down there is having something,

00:29:35.367 --> 00:29:36.817
"something's wrong with him."

00:29:39.814 --> 00:29:41.192
But it turned out good
Is there a grease stain

00:29:41.192 --> 00:29:43.867
on your concrete?

00:29:43.867 --> 00:29:45.836
Cause that's tough.

00:29:45.836 --> 00:29:46.850
You know what I did?

00:29:46.850 --> 00:29:50.800
I've had some oil mishaps
on this surface already.

00:29:50.800 --> 00:29:51.690
Okay.
So what I did

00:29:51.690 --> 00:29:54.210
is I took one of those bath towels

00:29:54.210 --> 00:29:57.990
and I polished the entire
surface with the peanut oil.

00:29:57.990 --> 00:29:59.740
Oh.
And it just evened it out.

00:30:01.460 --> 00:30:02.450
Like it never happened.

00:30:02.450 --> 00:30:03.440
I bet it smells good out here.

00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:04.876
It does. It smells great.

00:30:04.876 --> 00:30:08.880
Just don't smoke a cigarette out there

00:30:08.880 --> 00:30:10.290
You want to talk about Disneyland?

00:30:10.290 --> 00:30:11.480
Yeah.

00:30:11.480 --> 00:30:13.800
Yeah. So the first day we went to...

00:30:14.650 --> 00:30:17.570
I always want to call
it islands of Adventure,

00:30:17.570 --> 00:30:20.720
but that's the Universal thing.

00:30:20.720 --> 00:30:22.560
And because that was in my head,

00:30:22.560 --> 00:30:24.950
I can't call it the right thing.

00:30:24.950 --> 00:30:27.360
Where, when Mythical was smaller,

00:30:27.360 --> 00:30:28.597
we all went to--

00:30:29.465 --> 00:30:30.900
What's the car's place?

00:30:30.900 --> 00:30:33.690
What's it called? Adventure,
California Adventure,

00:30:33.690 --> 00:30:34.690
California Adventure.

00:30:34.690 --> 00:30:35.610
Yeah.
That's what it's called.

00:30:35.610 --> 00:30:36.840
Yeah.

00:30:36.840 --> 00:30:37.673
We went there on the first day

00:30:37.673 --> 00:30:40.459
and then we went to Disneyland proper,

00:30:40.459 --> 00:30:41.980
on the second day.

00:30:41.980 --> 00:30:45.720
I had not been to Islands of Adventure

00:30:45.720 --> 00:30:49.240
since California Adventure,

00:30:49.240 --> 00:30:50.900
I haven't been to the adventure.

00:30:50.900 --> 00:30:52.360
Yeah.
Since

00:30:52.360 --> 00:30:57.330
they made Avengers Campus a thing,

00:30:57.330 --> 00:30:59.280
there's a--
Where is that?

00:30:59.280 --> 00:31:01.270
You go in and you hang a left.

00:31:01.270 --> 00:31:02.410
Was it something else?

00:31:02.410 --> 00:31:04.620
It was something else
that wasn't memorable.

00:31:04.620 --> 00:31:05.530
And it had--

00:31:05.530 --> 00:31:07.130
It didn't replace Indiana Jones, right?

00:31:07.130 --> 00:31:08.010
Indiana Jones--
No, no, no,

00:31:08.010 --> 00:31:09.120
That's in Disneyland.

00:31:09.120 --> 00:31:14.060
So Tower of Terror has been revamped

00:31:14.060 --> 00:31:16.350
as a Guardians of the Galaxy ride.

00:31:16.350 --> 00:31:18.113
Oh, the ants, the Antworld

00:31:18.113 --> 00:31:19.980
Antworld.
That's gone.

00:31:19.980 --> 00:31:20.850
Ant's ride is gone.

00:31:20.850 --> 00:31:22.830
That was a big area that had like...

00:31:22.830 --> 00:31:24.687
You could walk through,
there're kids stuff

00:31:24.687 --> 00:31:26.510
Yeah, and you seem like...

00:31:26.510 --> 00:31:28.980
It was like, "Honey, I shrunk
the kids" kind of a vibe.

00:31:28.980 --> 00:31:30.050
It was time for that to go
Right.

00:31:30.050 --> 00:31:31.330
See, we never went there.

00:31:31.330 --> 00:31:33.100
They changed that into Avengers Campus,

00:31:33.100 --> 00:31:36.580
and then the pier part

00:31:36.580 --> 00:31:39.960
with the roller coaster
and the big Ferris wheel

00:31:39.960 --> 00:31:41.620
and the water.

00:31:41.620 --> 00:31:42.710
And the corn dog castles

00:31:42.710 --> 00:31:44.430
And the corn dog castle that you love.

00:31:44.430 --> 00:31:45.263
They're not getting rid of that.

00:31:45.263 --> 00:31:46.490
Corndog castle is still there.

00:31:46.490 --> 00:31:47.823
They're never getting rid of that.

00:31:47.823 --> 00:31:49.190
That's the pinnacle of the park.

00:31:49.190 --> 00:31:51.400
I almost got one, but I didn't.

00:31:51.400 --> 00:31:54.560
They changed that Pixar Pier.

00:31:54.560 --> 00:31:57.770
And then there's like those rides--

00:31:57.770 --> 00:31:59.970
So Carsland kinda got
extended out into the--

00:31:59.970 --> 00:32:03.030
Carsland is still its own thing.

00:32:03.030 --> 00:32:05.150
But I was most...

00:32:05.150 --> 00:32:06.970
I mean, we went to California Adventure

00:32:06.970 --> 00:32:09.850
and they made that rollercoaster

00:32:09.850 --> 00:32:12.720
into an incredible steamed rollercoaster,

00:32:12.720 --> 00:32:14.560
but it's the same rollercoaster.

00:32:14.560 --> 00:32:16.150
And Christy was very proud of herself

00:32:16.150 --> 00:32:17.140
cause she went on that,

00:32:17.140 --> 00:32:19.283
but she didn't tell us
how petrified she was,

00:32:19.283 --> 00:32:20.930
that she was overcoming something

00:32:20.930 --> 00:32:21.930
The wooden roller coaster.

00:32:21.930 --> 00:32:25.200
Yeah. Not a huge fan of it,
but it, but it was fine.

00:32:25.200 --> 00:32:27.550
But at the Avengers Campus,

00:32:27.550 --> 00:32:31.120
there's this brand new
Spider-Man ride that like...

00:32:31.120 --> 00:32:33.490
I don't know if you know,

00:32:33.490 --> 00:32:35.070
on Pixar Pier,

00:32:35.070 --> 00:32:40.070
there's a VR ride

00:32:40.330 --> 00:32:43.030
where you're playing
all these carnival games

00:32:43.030 --> 00:32:45.050
with 3D glasses on

00:32:45.050 --> 00:32:48.650
and it's like Pixar
Toy Story themed stuff.

00:32:48.650 --> 00:32:49.707
And that's really awesome.
That's been there a while.

00:32:49.707 --> 00:32:51.210
The one where you're shooting?

00:32:51.210 --> 00:32:52.770
Where you're shooting
rings and stuff and--

00:32:52.770 --> 00:32:54.160
Oh, that's amazing
Keeping the score.

00:32:54.160 --> 00:32:55.233
That's amazing.

00:32:56.150 --> 00:32:58.720
Well, they did a Spider-Man ride

00:32:58.720 --> 00:33:00.980
that is basically the same approach

00:33:00.980 --> 00:33:03.040
but instead of using a canon

00:33:03.040 --> 00:33:05.990
that you're actually pulling
on something physical

00:33:05.990 --> 00:33:09.900
and then these imaginary
3D rings are coming out,

00:33:09.900 --> 00:33:14.900
you just throw out your hand
as if you're casting a web,

00:33:15.290 --> 00:33:16.646
like you're Spider- Man,

00:33:16.646 --> 00:33:18.160
phew, phew, phew, phew.

00:33:18.160 --> 00:33:20.410
You don't have to make
the noises, but I did.

00:33:21.660 --> 00:33:22.920
And it just--
Did you feel

00:33:22.920 --> 00:33:24.220
like it's accurate?

00:33:24.220 --> 00:33:27.250
It's pretty accurate and
you're throwing 'em...

00:33:27.250 --> 00:33:29.760
And so you're on this track
and you're zinging around

00:33:29.760 --> 00:33:31.950
and there's all these set design,

00:33:31.950 --> 00:33:33.240
but then all these screens,

00:33:33.240 --> 00:33:35.640
and it's 3D glasses and all that.

00:33:35.640 --> 00:33:38.060
We waited for like an hour and a half

00:33:38.060 --> 00:33:39.193
to get on that ride.

00:33:40.177 --> 00:33:41.460
It's not worth more than an hour.

00:33:41.460 --> 00:33:43.760
They've done away with the Fast Pass,

00:33:43.760 --> 00:33:44.593
That's gone.

00:33:45.700 --> 00:33:47.400
Having been there now...

00:33:49.200 --> 00:33:50.840
Why did they get rid of the Fast Pass?

00:33:50.840 --> 00:33:52.130
It was just becoming clogged?

00:33:52.130 --> 00:33:53.960
I didn't research why.

00:33:53.960 --> 00:33:55.328
Is it like a traffic issue?

00:33:55.328 --> 00:33:56.610
Is everybody going to the Fast Pass?

00:33:56.610 --> 00:33:57.980
Who knows all of their reasons.

00:33:57.980 --> 00:34:00.870
But if you have an annual pass,

00:34:00.870 --> 00:34:02.530
you can then get something

00:34:02.530 --> 00:34:07.530
which will give you a
comparable experience

00:34:07.620 --> 00:34:09.660
to Fast Pass, I think.

00:34:09.660 --> 00:34:11.200
But because I couldn't get that

00:34:11.200 --> 00:34:13.260
and we don't have annual passes,

00:34:13.260 --> 00:34:14.730
we just waited in line.

00:34:14.730 --> 00:34:16.840
But that was way too long for Spider- Man,

00:34:16.840 --> 00:34:18.780
especially when halfway through the ride,

00:34:18.780 --> 00:34:21.300
I was so exhausted and I was pretty--

00:34:21.300 --> 00:34:22.133
Shoulder popped out.

00:34:22.133 --> 00:34:23.460
I thought my shoulder was gonna pop out.

00:34:23.460 --> 00:34:24.420
Right
Both of them,

00:34:24.420 --> 00:34:26.930
like I'd come out of the
thing just limp-armed.

00:34:26.930 --> 00:34:29.130
Just the rest of the day knuckle draggin.

00:34:29.130 --> 00:34:30.112
You gotta be careful

00:34:30.112 --> 00:34:32.040
when you got that Neal physiology.

00:34:32.040 --> 00:34:32.873
Right, Mm-hmm.

00:34:32.873 --> 00:34:33.730
Can't be Spider-Man.

00:34:33.730 --> 00:34:35.940
But the Tower of Terror turned

00:34:35.940 --> 00:34:39.120
into the Guardians of the
Galaxy ride was amazing.

00:34:39.120 --> 00:34:40.960
I woulda waited 90 minutes for that.

00:34:40.960 --> 00:34:42.650
Still works in the same fashion?

00:34:42.650 --> 00:34:43.600
Yes.

00:34:43.600 --> 00:34:44.840
Mechanically, it's this...

00:34:44.840 --> 00:34:47.970
You get on, basically an elevator.

00:34:47.970 --> 00:34:49.590
And then the doors open and...

00:34:49.590 --> 00:34:51.270
The elevators falling and rising,

00:34:51.270 --> 00:34:54.220
and the doors are opening
at different levels,

00:34:54.220 --> 00:34:57.800
and you're seeing different video screens.

00:34:57.800 --> 00:34:59.620
But the way that they themed it...

00:35:01.130 --> 00:35:03.480
In Guardians and in some
of the other Marvel movies,

00:35:03.480 --> 00:35:07.030
like Benicio Del Toro
played The Collector.

00:35:07.030 --> 00:35:09.640
And so they turned the whole thing

00:35:09.640 --> 00:35:11.570
into The Collector's museum.

00:35:11.570 --> 00:35:14.020
So when you're going through the line,

00:35:14.020 --> 00:35:15.700
there's like all these specimens,

00:35:15.700 --> 00:35:17.313
plant specimens,

00:35:18.810 --> 00:35:20.580
weaponry, all of this stuff

00:35:20.580 --> 00:35:22.080
from the Marvel cinematic universe

00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:23.170
that he's collected--

00:35:23.170 --> 00:35:25.870
To kinda make the line not as bad.

00:35:25.870 --> 00:35:26.980
Yeah.

00:35:26.980 --> 00:35:28.120
And that was cool.

00:35:28.120 --> 00:35:29.240
And then you get in there,

00:35:29.240 --> 00:35:32.460
and he's captured the guardians

00:35:32.460 --> 00:35:34.250
and then they're each on display.

00:35:34.250 --> 00:35:35.290
So then you've got to get them out

00:35:35.290 --> 00:35:36.320
by getting on the elevator.

00:35:36.320 --> 00:35:37.670
This is the main opening
And sitting there.

00:35:37.670 --> 00:35:39.310
Well, the premise is

00:35:39.310 --> 00:35:42.230
you're just there attending the opening

00:35:42.230 --> 00:35:46.100
of his new exhibit, which
is seeing the guardians.

00:35:46.100 --> 00:35:48.660
So it's really cool when
everything in the line

00:35:48.660 --> 00:35:50.280
and everything leading up to it does that,

00:35:50.280 --> 00:35:51.930
but then when you get in there,

00:35:51.930 --> 00:35:54.710
yeah like Rocket escapes.

00:35:54.710 --> 00:35:56.880
Is it the real actors doing all of it?

00:35:56.880 --> 00:35:59.280
Yeah. As far as I can
tell, it sounds like it.

00:35:59.280 --> 00:36:01.603
I think they've--
Oh, well yeah, definitely.

00:36:01.603 --> 00:36:04.410
There's footage of all of them.

00:36:04.410 --> 00:36:05.710
That's like for the ride.

00:36:05.710 --> 00:36:07.980
This point that's gotta
be in the contract.

00:36:07.980 --> 00:36:08.813
Yeah, I'm thinking so.
Cause you know

00:36:08.813 --> 00:36:09.920
back in the day,

00:36:09.920 --> 00:36:10.753
They didn't do it.

00:36:10.753 --> 00:36:12.490
You'd show up at the ride.

00:36:12.490 --> 00:36:13.323
I ain't doing no ride.

00:36:13.323 --> 00:36:16.381
It's like, "That's not Christopher Reeve."

00:36:17.480 --> 00:36:19.360
Right.
Or whatever it was.

00:36:19.360 --> 00:36:21.920
It's definitely what's his
name from Parks and Rec?

00:36:21.920 --> 00:36:23.020
Yep, Chris Pratt.

00:36:23.020 --> 00:36:23.900
Yeah, him.

00:36:23.900 --> 00:36:25.130
You couldn't remember Chris Pratt's name?

00:36:25.130 --> 00:36:27.500
You know, he's definitely in it,

00:36:27.500 --> 00:36:29.050
and Zoe Saldana.

00:36:29.050 --> 00:36:30.200
I'll remember her name any day that week.

00:36:30.200 --> 00:36:31.160
Yeah, right.

00:36:31.160 --> 00:36:32.130
And if you gave me her phone number,

00:36:32.130 --> 00:36:33.170
I'll remember that too.

00:36:33.170 --> 00:36:34.003
I doubt that.

00:36:34.003 --> 00:36:35.370
Nah, I wouldn't,

00:36:35.370 --> 00:36:36.930
I don't remember phone numbers anymore,

00:36:36.930 --> 00:36:38.390
you just store them in your phone.

00:36:38.390 --> 00:36:40.290
Yeah.
That was all a joke anyway.

00:36:42.950 --> 00:36:44.727
Anyway--
If you had to--

00:36:44.727 --> 00:36:46.340
The theme,
If you had to meet her,

00:36:46.340 --> 00:36:48.950
would you rather her be
as who she is or green?

00:36:48.950 --> 00:36:50.470
Oh, green. That would be awesome.

00:36:50.470 --> 00:36:51.303
Right.

00:36:51.303 --> 00:36:52.680
And then I'd know she really worked for it

00:36:52.680 --> 00:36:53.513
to meet me.

00:36:53.513 --> 00:36:56.160
It's like, "Oh, you put an hours."

00:36:56.160 --> 00:36:57.820
But just because I said
I wanted to meet them.

00:36:57.820 --> 00:36:58.990
I was on the jet bridge,

00:36:58.990 --> 00:36:59.823
The green version?
With her

00:36:59.823 --> 00:37:01.240
and her man one time.

00:37:01.240 --> 00:37:03.323
I remember that. You told me about it.

00:37:04.420 --> 00:37:06.110
That ride was thrilling.

00:37:06.110 --> 00:37:08.610
Again, it's the same ride physically,

00:37:08.610 --> 00:37:13.220
but I've never experienced the
theme being placed on a ride

00:37:13.220 --> 00:37:16.730
and it making it so much more satisfying.

00:37:16.730 --> 00:37:18.040
Yeah, and you know,
there's a lot of purists

00:37:18.040 --> 00:37:19.810
who get upset about that kind of thing.

00:37:19.810 --> 00:37:22.957
Who are like, "Tower of Terror's
been completely compromised

00:37:22.957 --> 00:37:25.000
"because they made it the Avengers ride."

00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:26.530
I don't see how anyone could complain

00:37:26.530 --> 00:37:29.140
because it's so much more amazing.

00:37:29.140 --> 00:37:30.630
And it's so, I mean that was--

00:37:30.630 --> 00:37:32.600
If it can be complained about, it will be.

00:37:32.600 --> 00:37:34.410
My second favorite ride.

00:37:34.410 --> 00:37:36.730
And then towards the end of the day,

00:37:36.730 --> 00:37:39.170
we timed to go in the Cars Line,

00:37:39.170 --> 00:37:41.570
which was over an hour.

00:37:41.570 --> 00:37:42.403
That's a good ride.

00:37:42.403 --> 00:37:45.000
But when the sun setting on that,

00:37:45.000 --> 00:37:47.580
the set design and that world is just,

00:37:47.580 --> 00:37:49.620
it holds up so many years later

00:37:49.620 --> 00:37:50.980
and it doesn't even matter if you've--

00:37:50.980 --> 00:37:52.130
It's like it's a real desert.

00:37:52.130 --> 00:37:55.430
If you've seen the
movie. It's so beautiful.

00:37:55.430 --> 00:37:56.277
And then you get on the ride

00:37:56.277 --> 00:37:58.160
and you're like, you're in the car.

00:37:58.160 --> 00:38:00.530
And your joy riding through this.

00:38:00.530 --> 00:38:01.770
And you're just looking around

00:38:01.770 --> 00:38:04.790
like, "I'm in monument valley."

00:38:04.790 --> 00:38:05.920
It never gets old.

00:38:05.920 --> 00:38:07.810
I love that.
It's so great.

00:38:07.810 --> 00:38:09.570
So that's my third favorite ride.

00:38:09.570 --> 00:38:10.450
But on the second day,

00:38:10.450 --> 00:38:11.380
we went to Disneyland.

00:38:11.380 --> 00:38:13.660
Hold on, so you didn't go on Soarin?

00:38:13.660 --> 00:38:14.591
We did go on Soarin.

00:38:15.483 --> 00:38:16.400
I love Soarin man.

00:38:16.400 --> 00:38:17.850
Soarin takes you around the world.

00:38:17.850 --> 00:38:18.802
I love it, man.

00:38:18.802 --> 00:38:21.248
It's not just California Soarin.

00:38:21.248 --> 00:38:22.947
It takes you around the world.

00:38:22.947 --> 00:38:24.290
And you smell things.

00:38:24.290 --> 00:38:25.410
And you smell stuff.

00:38:25.410 --> 00:38:26.490
What kinda stuff you smell now?

00:38:26.490 --> 00:38:28.570
Oh man, I gotta go back
Grass.

00:38:28.570 --> 00:38:29.403
You smell grass?

00:38:29.403 --> 00:38:31.808
When they went over the orange fields,

00:38:31.808 --> 00:38:32.928
in Soarin
You don't smell any orange

00:38:32.928 --> 00:38:33.898
The citrus spray?

00:38:33.898 --> 00:38:35.130
You're wearing a mask now.

00:38:35.130 --> 00:38:36.750
You've gotta wear a mask inside,

00:38:36.750 --> 00:38:37.980
with all this pandemic stuff.

00:38:37.980 --> 00:38:39.590
Have you heard about it?

00:38:39.590 --> 00:38:41.753
So you're wearing a mask
Something's going around.

00:38:43.120 --> 00:38:46.220
You wearing a mask the
whole time you're in Disney?

00:38:46.220 --> 00:38:47.903
No, just inside.
Or just when you go inside.

00:38:49.305 --> 00:38:50.820
Just inside.
Is a rollercoaster

00:38:50.820 --> 00:38:52.073
considered inside?

00:38:54.210 --> 00:38:56.170
Like Space Mountain's inside a mountain.

00:38:56.170 --> 00:38:57.003
No,

00:38:57.003 --> 00:38:57.836
I think you're moving too fast

00:38:57.836 --> 00:38:59.660
for the virus at that point,

00:38:59.660 --> 00:39:01.000
It can't keep up with the rollercoaster.

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:02.600
Well, Space Mountain, I didn't ride that.

00:39:02.600 --> 00:39:03.433
So I don't know if they
made you wear the mask,

00:39:03.433 --> 00:39:05.470
because that is indoors.

00:39:05.470 --> 00:39:06.670
You probably did have to wear the mask.

00:39:06.670 --> 00:39:07.520
But I won't know.

00:39:09.150 --> 00:39:11.387
The second day I was like,

00:39:11.387 --> 00:39:14.757
"As long as I can ride the
Rise of the Resistance,

00:39:14.757 --> 00:39:16.770
"which I have never ridden,"

00:39:16.770 --> 00:39:19.060
I have been Galaxy's Edge.

00:39:19.060 --> 00:39:21.340
Like the Star Wars world.

00:39:21.340 --> 00:39:23.460
I thought you rode it
the first time you went?

00:39:23.460 --> 00:39:26.370
No, just the Millennium Falcon ride,

00:39:26.370 --> 00:39:27.480
but Rise of Resistance,

00:39:27.480 --> 00:39:29.600
But it wasn't done when--
Lily had been on it but...

00:39:29.600 --> 00:39:31.470
No, they wasn't even talking about it

00:39:31.470 --> 00:39:32.523
the last time I went.

00:39:33.420 --> 00:39:36.380
And of course this ride
is built up so much

00:39:36.380 --> 00:39:38.137
to the point where I'm like,

00:39:38.137 --> 00:39:39.887
"Okay, I know that it says

00:39:39.887 --> 00:39:43.807
"that it's a two hour wait for this ride,

00:39:43.807 --> 00:39:48.807
"but this is the best theme
ride on the planet potentially,"

00:39:50.260 --> 00:39:51.800
from everything I've heard.

00:39:51.800 --> 00:39:54.277
So I'm not gonna wig out about it.

00:39:54.277 --> 00:39:56.620
I'm just gonna get in line.

00:39:56.620 --> 00:40:01.080
And first of all, talk about
the lines and the walking,

00:40:01.080 --> 00:40:02.701
like--
You're not ready for this.

00:40:02.701 --> 00:40:04.360
I was not ready

00:40:04.360 --> 00:40:05.350
You need a pair of wheelies

00:40:05.350 --> 00:40:07.940
For being on my feet all...

