Christy sent a picture
of you to our group chat.

00:40:25.700 --> 00:40:26.850
And you were just sleeping.

00:40:26.850 --> 00:40:28.200
I was sitting up.

00:40:28.200 --> 00:40:29.560
No, there was one where
you were lying down

00:40:29.560 --> 00:40:31.510
Yeah, I ended up lying down.

00:40:31.510 --> 00:40:32.430
It was like...

00:40:32.430 --> 00:40:36.460
Well, first I took my I took
my shoes and my socks off.

00:40:36.460 --> 00:40:39.318
And she was like, "This is a restaurant."

00:40:39.318 --> 00:40:40.977
And I was like, "This isn't a restaurant.

00:40:40.977 --> 00:40:42.890
"This is just some tables outside."

00:40:42.890 --> 00:40:44.840
But what if everyone did what you did.

00:40:44.840 --> 00:40:47.970
What if everyone took their
shoes and socks off at Disney--

00:40:47.970 --> 00:40:50.490
I saw a few other people doing it.

00:40:50.490 --> 00:40:52.280
So it's not like something I invented.

00:40:52.280 --> 00:40:53.380
Okay.
Lemme tell you.

00:40:53.380 --> 00:40:54.790
I was in a corner,

00:40:54.790 --> 00:40:57.040
on my right was nothing but plants.

00:40:57.040 --> 00:40:59.310
There was talk about escorting you out,

00:40:59.310 --> 00:41:00.250
just so you know,

00:41:00.250 --> 00:41:03.700
between Herb from Omaha, Nebraska

00:41:03.700 --> 00:41:07.380
and Dale from St. Louis, Missouri.

00:41:07.380 --> 00:41:08.930
Cause it says it on their nametag.

00:41:08.930 --> 00:41:09.763
They were like,

00:41:10.987 --> 00:41:11.847
"we have a barefoot.

00:41:11.847 --> 00:41:13.960
"We have a barefoot situation."

00:41:13.960 --> 00:41:15.750
I mean, people walking around in sandals.

00:41:15.750 --> 00:41:17.340
We'll give them another seven minutes.

00:41:17.340 --> 00:41:19.940
People kick off their sandals.

00:41:19.940 --> 00:41:22.500
I just kicked off my shoes and my socks

00:41:22.500 --> 00:41:23.333
and I needed to man.

00:41:23.333 --> 00:41:27.752
Kicking off socks is never
good man for everybody else.

00:41:29.780 --> 00:41:30.613
I'm sure it was good.

00:41:30.613 --> 00:41:32.140
I felt bad, but I was desperate.

00:41:32.140 --> 00:41:32.973
And then I was like,

00:41:32.973 --> 00:41:34.570
I just have--
This is day one?

00:41:34.570 --> 00:41:36.200
Day one. I was hurting man.

00:41:36.200 --> 00:41:39.020
And I was just sitting there and then,

00:41:39.020 --> 00:41:40.260
it was a chair,.

00:41:40.260 --> 00:41:42.960
And then once they got up and left,

00:41:42.960 --> 00:41:45.340
then I moved over two more chairs

00:41:45.340 --> 00:41:47.320
and then I just laid down

00:41:47.320 --> 00:41:49.400
and literally went to sleep

00:41:49.400 --> 00:41:50.560
for at least 20 minutes,

00:41:50.560 --> 00:41:52.510
and boy I needed every second of that.

00:41:52.510 --> 00:41:54.470
This makes me think about,

00:41:54.470 --> 00:41:56.470
there's a couple of
potential modifications

00:41:56.470 --> 00:41:57.840
that they can make to the line.

00:41:57.840 --> 00:41:59.820
Now obviously they're doing a lot

00:41:59.820 --> 00:42:02.530
to make the line more entertaining

00:42:02.530 --> 00:42:06.400
because they're making
it as museum or whatever.

00:42:06.400 --> 00:42:08.777
So there's interest factor along the way.

00:42:08.777 --> 00:42:10.080
But that only goes so far.

00:42:10.080 --> 00:42:10.913
Two ideas.

00:42:10.913 --> 00:42:13.670
Number one, is provide a way
for people to just lie down

00:42:13.670 --> 00:42:15.470
and slowly be pushed,

00:42:15.470 --> 00:42:16.303
I love that idea

00:42:16.303 --> 00:42:17.210
Take your shoes and socks off,

00:42:17.210 --> 00:42:18.550
and just slowly be pushed.

00:42:18.550 --> 00:42:20.690
Some people are in those motorized carts,

00:42:20.690 --> 00:42:21.830
but why can't everyone?

00:42:21.830 --> 00:42:22.730
But just something...

00:42:22.730 --> 00:42:25.190
Yeah, I mean something for everyone

00:42:25.190 --> 00:42:27.160
that doesn't take up too much room.

00:42:27.160 --> 00:42:29.110
Second potential option.

00:42:29.110 --> 00:42:31.890
And I know there's people who
take this into their own hands

00:42:31.890 --> 00:42:34.030
and they come up with like a game to play

00:42:34.030 --> 00:42:35.500
while they're in line.

00:42:35.500 --> 00:42:36.750
I kind of feel like--

00:42:36.750 --> 00:42:37.583
Yeah, the heads...

00:42:37.583 --> 00:42:39.150
A lot of people were
playing the heads up game.

00:42:39.150 --> 00:42:43.900
But maybe Disney could actually Create

00:42:43.900 --> 00:42:45.730
Line games
Line games.

00:42:45.730 --> 00:42:46.880
That's a good idea.

00:42:46.880 --> 00:42:48.320
And they bring them to you.

00:42:48.320 --> 00:42:51.120
I know an Imagineer
who works in the parks.

00:42:51.120 --> 00:42:53.400
I mean, I could make a phone call

00:42:53.400 --> 00:42:56.910
and I could suggest this
and then maybe get 10%.

00:42:56.910 --> 00:42:58.600
I saw the people doing heads up,

00:42:58.600 --> 00:43:00.970
and then I just felt like,

00:43:00.970 --> 00:43:03.420
if I did that, it wouldn't
be an original idea.

00:43:03.420 --> 00:43:05.297
As a family, we never even
talked about doing it.

00:43:05.297 --> 00:43:09.610
But if you're in the Star Wars ride line,

00:43:09.610 --> 00:43:12.360
this is the game that
you can play in the line.

00:43:12.360 --> 00:43:13.450
And it's just like...

00:43:15.100 --> 00:43:17.740
The line is suited to it somehow.

00:43:17.740 --> 00:43:20.760
I did notice the one thing that they did

00:43:20.760 --> 00:43:23.960
even when the line was like 90 minutes

00:43:23.960 --> 00:43:26.290
and that's really what
Rise of Resistance was

00:43:26.290 --> 00:43:27.150
once we got in it.

00:43:27.150 --> 00:43:30.720
Now I will say it ended
up only being an hour.

00:43:30.720 --> 00:43:33.970
So it moved faster.

00:43:33.970 --> 00:43:35.003
The thing I noticed was--

00:43:35.003 --> 00:43:36.500
That was manipulation.

00:43:36.500 --> 00:43:40.410
Yeah, they raise the bar and
then they make you happy.

00:43:40.410 --> 00:43:44.050
Yeah. Low expectations man

00:43:44.050 --> 00:43:46.960
The line never stopped moving.

00:43:46.960 --> 00:43:48.642
It wasn't stop and start,

00:43:48.642 --> 00:43:49.475
stop and start.

00:43:50.470 --> 00:43:54.140
And there were even some
benches placed along the way,

00:43:54.140 --> 00:43:55.640
but because the line never stopped,

00:43:55.640 --> 00:43:57.290
you couldn't sit on a bench.

00:43:57.290 --> 00:43:58.550
So I found that interesting,

00:43:58.550 --> 00:44:00.970
but it did help a lot psychologically,

00:44:00.970 --> 00:44:04.500
but what it didn't help
with was like by day two,

00:44:04.500 --> 00:44:06.400
when it was my nap time again,

00:44:06.400 --> 00:44:07.690
here I am in this line

00:44:07.690 --> 00:44:10.300
and I can't even sit down for a second.

00:44:10.300 --> 00:44:12.400
So, and I'm just...

00:44:12.400 --> 00:44:15.200
My hip flexor is just hurting.

00:44:15.200 --> 00:44:16.033
You're talking...

00:44:16.033 --> 00:44:18.190
First of all, you started off this episode

00:44:18.190 --> 00:44:21.760
talking about your physical form,

00:44:21.760 --> 00:44:24.080
or your physical peak or whatever.

00:44:24.080 --> 00:44:24.913
Yeah that was a setup,

00:44:24.913 --> 00:44:25.890
this is the payoff.

00:44:25.890 --> 00:44:26.863
Oh, okay. Got it.

00:44:28.530 --> 00:44:32.090
And so the only thing
that would give me relief

00:44:32.090 --> 00:44:33.520
was deep squats.

00:44:33.520 --> 00:44:35.570
Like if I really squatted down,

00:44:35.570 --> 00:44:38.030
my hips would open up a little bit

00:44:38.030 --> 00:44:40.010
and I'd start to feel better.

00:44:40.010 --> 00:44:43.140
But the line wouldn't stop so I had to...

00:44:43.140 --> 00:44:45.210
And I didn't wanna just
keep squatting down

00:44:45.210 --> 00:44:47.020
and squatting up.

00:44:47.020 --> 00:44:48.980
So when I squatted down
and the line moved,

00:44:48.980 --> 00:44:53.900
then I just started duck
walking behind the line.

00:44:55.020 --> 00:44:57.550
And I experienced lots of relief

00:44:57.550 --> 00:44:59.810
