I get nervous in the lines

01:00:54.670 --> 01:00:56.270
because it's nice...

01:00:56.270 --> 01:00:59.123
I like it when I see
people who recognize me,

01:01:00.210 --> 01:01:02.330
there's like a shudder.

01:01:02.330 --> 01:01:03.680
It's like, Hey, it feels...

01:01:04.560 --> 01:01:05.950
It's kinda cool.

01:01:05.950 --> 01:01:07.820
A lot of people don't get
to experience that moment

01:01:07.820 --> 01:01:10.200
of like seeing somebody see you

01:01:10.200 --> 01:01:13.660
and they kind of have this
like physical response.

01:01:13.660 --> 01:01:14.840
Yeah
And then

01:01:14.840 --> 01:01:17.550
the line keeps moving so they
can't do anything about it,

01:01:17.550 --> 01:01:19.150
so they're like...

01:01:19.150 --> 01:01:21.860
It's like they're just kinda
standing there, shell shocked.

01:01:21.860 --> 01:01:24.670
Cause it's the only way
when somebody meets you

01:01:24.670 --> 01:01:27.140
that you have permission to just walk away

01:01:27.140 --> 01:01:28.380
without saying anything.

01:01:28.380 --> 01:01:30.500
So I kind of enjoy that
when being in line,

01:01:30.500 --> 01:01:35.051
but then you see them
500 times after that.

01:01:35.051 --> 01:01:37.300
So they do have the opportunity

01:01:37.300 --> 01:01:41.470
to get the stuff together
so they can say hello.

01:01:41.470 --> 01:01:42.770
Yeah, and again,

01:01:42.770 --> 01:01:45.910
I don't think it's
possible to talk about this

01:01:45.910 --> 01:01:47.750
without seeming like a douche bag

01:01:47.750 --> 01:01:50.130
because it's not a very
relatable experience

01:01:50.130 --> 01:01:52.130
to get recognized.

01:01:52.130 --> 01:01:54.730
So I acknowledged that it's just...

01:01:54.730 --> 01:01:57.910
And I do appreciate it

01:01:57.910 --> 01:01:59.420
and I don't mind people approaching,

01:01:59.420 --> 01:02:02.750
but it's just like there
are certain circumstances

01:02:02.750 --> 01:02:06.020
in which it's especially inconvenient,

01:02:06.020 --> 01:02:07.450
especially for other people

01:02:07.450 --> 01:02:10.300
who are tryna get something done.

01:02:10.300 --> 01:02:13.300
And in those circumstances...

01:02:15.170 --> 01:02:16.730
Again, I was nice.

01:02:16.730 --> 01:02:18.330
I didn't, and then I didn't...

01:02:18.330 --> 01:02:21.070
I almost apologized to the
line of people as I left,

01:02:21.070 --> 01:02:22.678
but I was just like,
"I'm just gonna leave".

01:02:22.678 --> 01:02:24.270
Man just get out of there.

01:02:24.270 --> 01:02:25.103
I'll just leave.

01:02:25.103 --> 01:02:26.870
Just get out of there.

01:02:26.870 --> 01:02:30.030
Disneyland. That was great.

01:02:30.030 --> 01:02:31.330
It was great for Lily to be home

01:02:31.330 --> 01:02:32.740
and for us to do something as a family,

01:02:32.740 --> 01:02:34.840
because she had a number of people to see.

01:02:36.220 --> 01:02:37.540
You know, to reconnect with her friends

01:02:37.540 --> 01:02:39.450
and stuff like that
for the handful of days

01:02:39.450 --> 01:02:40.713
that she was back home.

01:02:41.570 --> 01:02:43.500
So it gave us our dedicated time,

01:02:43.500 --> 01:02:44.760
because then once we got back,

01:02:44.760 --> 01:02:46.730
we did the Thanksgiving lunch,

01:02:46.730 --> 01:02:47.640
but then after that,

01:02:47.640 --> 01:02:51.330
she was kinda gone seeing other people,

01:02:51.330 --> 01:02:53.910
which we totally expected and understood.

01:02:53.910 --> 01:02:56.200
And then she's back off at college,

01:02:56.200 --> 01:02:58.440
but only just for a couple of weeks

01:02:58.440 --> 01:03:00.610
before the Christmas break.

01:03:00.610 --> 01:03:03.850
So it was a great experience
being reconnected,

01:03:03.850 --> 01:03:06.220
especially cause like we all got along

01:03:06.220 --> 01:03:08.740
because we were in the
happiest place on earth

01:03:08.740 --> 01:03:10.233
and I wasn't in charge.

01:03:11.700 --> 01:03:13.903
Big factor.
I think that really worked.

01:03:14.890 --> 01:03:18.680
So yeah, it was a success.

01:03:18.680 --> 01:03:19.970
Last thing I'll share

01:03:19.970 --> 01:03:24.970
is that usually the
day after Thanksgiving,

01:03:25.780 --> 01:03:27.050
we go and get a Christmas tree.

01:03:27.050 --> 01:03:29.050
Aha,
We didn't

01:03:29.050 --> 01:03:32.223
because the family was
hanging on by a thread.

01:03:33.350 --> 01:03:34.870
You know, they're dropping like flies

01:03:34.870 --> 01:03:36.010
and I'm just trying not to get sick

01:03:36.010 --> 01:03:40.910
so Jessie was in no mood to go get a tree.

01:03:40.910 --> 01:03:42.460
And we had decorated a little bit

01:03:42.460 --> 01:03:44.590
before everybody got there with like...

01:03:44.590 --> 01:03:45.740
There's multiple trees.

01:03:48.952 --> 01:03:50.830
There's like four Christmas
trees in our house,

01:03:50.830 --> 01:03:52.520
but not...

01:03:52.520 --> 01:03:53.353
And they're small.

01:03:53.353 --> 01:03:54.760
Like the kids have little ones

01:03:54.760 --> 01:03:55.710
and I'm not talking big--

01:03:55.710 --> 01:03:58.000
So you're not gonna do
a real one this year?

01:03:58.000 --> 01:04:01.210
So Jessie's like, "We gotta
go get the real tree."

01:04:01.210 --> 01:04:04.210
And I'm like doing the
math on this and thinking,

01:04:04.210 --> 01:04:07.000
so we're gonna put this tree up,

01:04:07.000 --> 01:04:09.890
and then we're going back
home to North Carolina,

01:04:09.890 --> 01:04:11.290
like mid December.

01:04:11.290 --> 01:04:12.123
Yeah.

01:04:12.123 --> 01:04:13.380
And then we're not gonna be back

01:04:13.380 --> 01:04:14.963
until after the New Year.

01:04:16.135 --> 01:04:19.000
And it's like, we're not
gonna have anybody else over.

01:04:19.000 --> 01:04:22.890
And I just start realizing
how much of a Scrooge I am

01:04:22.890 --> 01:04:24.880
when it comes to the decorations,

01:04:24.880 --> 01:04:26.830
cause I'm like the decorations just feel

01:04:26.830 --> 01:04:31.770
like they're for us by us

01:04:31.770 --> 01:04:32.940
You know what I'm saying?

01:04:32.940 --> 01:04:36.580
And so it's like the bias part

01:04:36.580 --> 01:04:38.400
is the part that I have trouble with.

01:04:38.400 --> 01:04:40.173
Cause I'm like, "Oh, we're
gonna have to get this thing--"

01:04:40.173 --> 01:04:41.113
If it's just for you.

01:04:41.113 --> 01:04:42.913
We have to do the lights,

01:04:44.391 --> 01:04:45.617
but she's like, "But for the kids,

01:04:45.617 --> 01:04:47.120
"it's Locke's last Christmas here."

01:04:47.120 --> 01:04:49.417
I'm like, "Well, there's lots
of Christmas decorations.

01:04:49.417 --> 01:04:52.330
"There's multiple trees.
He's got one in his room."

01:04:52.330 --> 01:04:54.320
We haven't yet gotten the tree.

01:04:54.320 --> 01:04:55.910
I almost talked her into--

01:04:55.910 --> 01:04:57.470
But there are other trees in other places,

01:04:57.470 --> 01:04:58.303
but just not...

01:04:58.303 --> 01:04:59.136
you don't have a main tree.

01:04:59.136 --> 01:05:01.189
We don't have a main real
tree that we put in--

01:05:01.189 --> 01:05:02.350
You sound like my dad, man.

01:05:02.350 --> 01:05:03.183
They've got--

01:05:03.183 --> 01:05:05.480
I mean, Halloween, they
decorated for Christmas.

01:05:05.480 --> 01:05:07.630
They got like eight trees.

01:05:07.630 --> 01:05:08.980
It's like they live for it.

01:05:09.877 --> 01:05:11.100
We got one tree.

01:05:11.100 --> 01:05:12.180
Jessie loves it.

01:05:12.180 --> 01:05:13.910
I appreciate...

01:05:13.910 --> 01:05:16.900
Listen, again, I experienced the benefit

01:05:16.900 --> 01:05:18.370
because I didn't help with that.

01:05:18.370 --> 01:05:22.340
All I did was went into
the attic and pushed...

01:05:22.340 --> 01:05:23.173
My back was already messed up

01:05:23.173 --> 01:05:26.170
so I was pushing the boxes to the entrance

01:05:26.170 --> 01:05:27.983
and then Locke was taking them down.

01:05:29.610 --> 01:05:31.720
And then Jessie is taking this stuff out.

01:05:31.720 --> 01:05:33.510
But I don't know.

01:05:33.510 --> 01:05:35.760
I think we may have passed
the point of no return

01:05:35.760 --> 01:05:36.880
for having a tree.

01:05:36.880 --> 01:05:38.607
And then I'm like, "But if we do get one,

01:05:38.607 --> 01:05:40.500
"let's get a fake pre-lit tree."

01:05:40.500 --> 01:05:41.930
And, listen, I know the
arguments against it.

01:05:41.930 --> 01:05:44.847
That's what we have now,
that's what we got last year.

01:05:44.847 --> 01:05:46.630
And so here's my question.
I love it.

01:05:46.630 --> 01:05:47.950
You take it out and you--

01:05:47.950 --> 01:05:50.690
How hard is it to put together?

01:05:50.690 --> 01:05:53.320
Easy, three sections

01:05:53.320 --> 01:05:55.360
and it's there and then it falls down

01:05:55.360 --> 01:05:56.193
and then that's it.

01:05:56.193 --> 01:05:57.407
And then you're like,

01:05:57.407 --> 01:05:59.240
"This is disappointing."

01:05:59.240 --> 01:06:01.750
And then you start hearing the complaints.

01:06:01.750 --> 01:06:03.360
It's not a real, it's too short,

01:06:03.360 --> 01:06:04.520
It's not this. It's not that.

01:06:04.520 --> 01:06:06.397
And then it's like, "But just decorate it.

01:06:06.397 --> 01:06:07.417
"And once you decorate it,

01:06:07.417 --> 01:06:08.250
"it's fine."
It's fine.

01:06:08.250 --> 01:06:09.293
It's fine. You know.

01:06:10.410 --> 01:06:14.250
Because all that happens
is the tree basically...

01:06:14.250 --> 01:06:16.240
Cause I do all this
stuff to take care of it,

01:06:16.240 --> 01:06:18.300
then it basically dies before we leave.

01:06:18.300 --> 01:06:20.680
Yeah.
Stops taking water,

01:06:20.680 --> 01:06:23.113
and then we get back and it's dead.

01:06:24.187 --> 01:06:27.180
And just taking the stuff off of the tree,

01:06:27.180 --> 01:06:29.190
causes all the little
needles to go everywhere.

01:06:29.190 --> 01:06:30.500
And then you got to take it out

01:06:30.500 --> 01:06:32.210
and put it down next to the...

01:06:32.210 --> 01:06:35.140
You nearly kill whoever
you're trying to do this with,

01:06:35.140 --> 01:06:36.320
trying to get it to the curb.

01:06:36.320 --> 01:06:37.910
I mean are there...

01:06:37.910 --> 01:06:39.810
Yeah, I'm with you man.

01:06:39.810 --> 01:06:40.670
But I know I'm like,

01:06:40.670 --> 01:06:42.490
are there pre-decorated trees.

01:06:42.490 --> 01:06:43.990
You got pre-lit.

01:06:43.990 --> 01:06:46.590
It's like, can you go all
the way, pre-decorated.

01:06:46.590 --> 01:06:47.820
You know, just pull out of the boxes.

01:06:47.820 --> 01:06:48.870
Jessie's not gonna for that.

01:06:48.870 --> 01:06:51.760
You know, it's just like. It's all done.

01:06:51.760 --> 01:06:52.840
I will say,

01:06:52.840 --> 01:06:57.840
the only thing that I usually
help with is the lights,

01:06:58.030 --> 01:06:59.900
which is the worst part

01:06:59.900 --> 01:07:02.090
and the top of the tree.

01:07:02.090 --> 01:07:04.380
Yeah, I could see why
And so

01:07:04.380 --> 01:07:06.860
if the lights are pre-lit I
don't have to worry about that.

01:07:06.860 --> 01:07:08.710
I'll put the three sections together.

01:07:08.710 --> 01:07:10.603
Are your other trees not pre-lit?

01:07:11.730 --> 01:07:13.280
You don't know cause you didn't do those.

01:07:13.280 --> 01:07:14.113
I don't...

01:07:14.113 --> 01:07:14.946
They're all fake.

01:07:14.946 --> 01:07:17.420
Okay, they better be
pre-lit you don't wanna...

01:07:17.420 --> 01:07:19.100
I don't think they're a pre-lit.

01:07:19.100 --> 01:07:21.270
We're not in the 90s anymore, okay.

01:07:21.270 --> 01:07:22.850
Wake up
So anyway, I kind of...

01:07:22.850 --> 01:07:24.290
I love Christmas,

01:07:24.290 --> 01:07:25.840
I love the holidays,

01:07:25.840 --> 01:07:27.400
I like the decorations.

01:07:27.400 --> 01:07:28.233
Yeah.

01:07:28.233 --> 01:07:29.870
But I'm a little bit of a Scrooge

01:07:29.870 --> 01:07:31.467
when I'm like,

01:07:31.467 --> 01:07:33.010
"Why are we doing this?"

01:07:33.010 --> 01:07:34.610
If we were going to be
here through Christmas

01:07:34.610 --> 01:07:36.640
and the whole time, we had a
bunch of people coming over,

01:07:36.640 --> 01:07:37.632
Right.

01:07:37.632 --> 01:07:39.060
That's not happening.

01:07:39.060 --> 01:07:41.717
So am I a Scrooge?

01:07:41.717 --> 01:07:42.960
#Earbiscuits?

01:07:42.960 --> 01:07:44.633
Yeah. I might give a rec.

01:07:46.250 --> 01:07:47.900
I've been really looking forward

01:07:47.900 --> 01:07:52.900
to the Peter Jackson
directed Beatles docu-series,

01:07:55.470 --> 01:07:57.230
it's called "Get Back."

01:07:57.230 --> 01:08:01.470
And I always think that it's on Apple,

01:08:01.470 --> 01:08:03.360
but it's on Disney plus.

01:08:03.360 --> 01:08:04.680
Yeah.
Cause I looked forever.

01:08:04.680 --> 01:08:07.686
I looked all over Apple
and I couldn't find it.

01:08:07.686 --> 01:08:09.490
You're looking in the wrong place..

01:08:09.490 --> 01:08:13.010
I will say I've only watched

01:08:13.010 --> 01:08:14.900
like an hour and a half of it,

01:08:14.900 --> 01:08:17.530
which is not much more than half

01:08:17.530 --> 01:08:18.775
of the first three episodes.

01:08:18.775 --> 01:08:21.000
Is it six hours total or something?

01:08:21.000 --> 01:08:23.887
Yeah. It's like he really
Peter Jacksoned it.

01:08:23.887 --> 01:08:28.887
So it's the footage leading
up to their last performance.

01:08:32.300 --> 01:08:36.180
But they didn't know that
at the time of course.

01:08:36.180 --> 01:08:37.930
It was just their first performance

01:08:37.930 --> 01:08:39.440
in more than two years

01:08:39.440 --> 01:08:42.960
that they were gonna
develop new material for,

01:08:42.960 --> 01:08:46.633
to perform for a TV special.

01:08:48.254 --> 01:08:49.720
And then they had a documentary crew,

01:08:49.720 --> 01:08:51.090
which that's what this footage is from.

01:08:51.090 --> 01:08:53.220
It's like film documentary,

01:08:53.220 --> 01:08:54.830
and then the release of the album,

01:08:54.830 --> 01:08:58.520
which became the, "Let it be" album.

01:08:58.520 --> 01:09:00.040
If I'm correct. I believe I am.

01:09:00.040 --> 01:09:04.270
So we heard some good stuff about it.

01:09:04.270 --> 01:09:05.520
We actually went to a restaurant,

01:09:05.520 --> 01:09:07.680
and they said, "How
was your Thanksgiving?"

01:09:07.680 --> 01:09:10.017
And the waiter said, "It was great.

01:09:10.017 --> 01:09:12.927
"I watched the Beatles docu-series

01:09:12.927 --> 01:09:14.250
"and I loved it."

01:09:14.250 --> 01:09:15.480
That's apparently all he did.

01:09:15.480 --> 01:09:16.780
And I was like, "Oh, it's out."

01:09:16.780 --> 01:09:18.080
and I was so excited.

01:09:18.080 --> 01:09:19.720
Everyone was talking about it on Twitter,

01:09:19.720 --> 01:09:21.410
about how amazing it was.

01:09:21.410 --> 01:09:26.410
It's a test of patience and a fandom.

01:09:26.500 --> 01:09:29.680
So I'm giving this recommendation couch

01:09:29.680 --> 01:09:32.480
and it's not for everybody

01:09:32.480 --> 01:09:34.390
because it's just a...

01:09:34.390 --> 01:09:37.720
But if you're really into it
is it's an amazing experience,

01:09:37.720 --> 01:09:39.240
but don't watch it when you're sleepy,

01:09:39.240 --> 01:09:41.333
because it's a fly on the wall,

01:09:43.160 --> 01:09:47.810
just footage of them, trying
to pull together physically,

01:09:47.810 --> 01:09:49.580
like be in the same space again

01:09:49.580 --> 01:09:51.280
and start to write songs.

01:09:51.280 --> 01:09:52.920
They're bringing material together

01:09:52.920 --> 01:09:54.560
and they're starting to play.

01:09:54.560 --> 01:09:56.660
And there's these...

01:09:57.800 --> 01:10:02.800
I get goosebumps talking about
the flashes of creativity

01:10:03.400 --> 01:10:06.900
where you see Paul McCartney showing up

01:10:06.900 --> 01:10:08.380
and George and Ringo in there.

01:10:08.380 --> 01:10:09.950
John's not even there yet,

01:10:09.950 --> 01:10:14.060
and then he starts writing "Get Back."

01:10:14.060 --> 01:10:16.351
Mm-hmm
No, no, no, no, no,

01:10:16.351 --> 01:10:18.250
no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

01:10:18.250 --> 01:10:19.830
You know, he's like...

01:10:19.830 --> 01:10:24.410
The genesis of that song
was fully documented

01:10:24.410 --> 01:10:27.480
in that environment under
all of this pressure

01:10:27.480 --> 01:10:29.060
and you see all of their personalities

01:10:29.060 --> 01:10:30.000
and their interactions.

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:31.840
And I get the impression that

01:10:31.840 --> 01:10:35.330
there's not footage like
this of them that exists

01:10:35.330 --> 01:10:36.930
because everybody's talking about,

01:10:36.930 --> 01:10:40.847
like, I saw Mark Marin tweet,

01:10:40.847 --> 01:10:44.480
"They're the guys I always
thought they would be."

01:10:44.480 --> 01:10:45.439
but like...

01:10:45.439 --> 01:10:47.190
Yes, yes.
And as a huge fan.

01:10:47.190 --> 01:10:48.740
There's just, no one has seen--

01:10:48.740 --> 01:10:50.710
But I've never hung
out with them like this

01:10:51.650 --> 01:10:52.877
Yeah, and people are talking about...

01:10:52.877 --> 01:10:55.550
and I've only watched
half of the first one.

01:10:55.550 --> 01:10:58.583
and then there's some things
that really start to happen.

01:10:59.510 --> 01:11:03.330
Like I know that George leaves,

01:11:03.330 --> 01:11:07.250
he quits the band in the midst of this.

01:11:07.250 --> 01:11:09.240
So it gets really good, but it's like,

01:11:09.240 --> 01:11:11.090
you really have to be committed to it

01:11:12.470 --> 01:11:14.240
and you have to be attentive

01:11:14.240 --> 01:11:19.240
to the points where the
magic of those moments

01:11:20.350 --> 01:11:24.700
is really set up by kinda
like the fly on the wall,

01:11:24.700 --> 01:11:28.660
20 minutes of them just interacting.

01:11:28.660 --> 01:11:31.090
So it's...

01:11:31.090 --> 01:11:33.160
At first I had tears in my eyes,

01:11:33.160 --> 01:11:34.860
and then I got bored.

01:11:34.860 --> 01:11:37.700
So it's a little bit of both,

01:11:37.700 --> 01:11:38.660
but if you push through,

01:11:38.660 --> 01:11:40.130
there's these there's these moments

01:11:40.130 --> 01:11:42.230
that are just captured,

01:11:42.230 --> 01:11:43.940
based on what I've already seen,

01:11:43.940 --> 01:11:45.790
that are probably extraordinary.

01:11:45.790 --> 01:11:47.860
And it does go, it does go somewhere.

01:11:47.860 --> 01:11:48.693
It's just,

01:11:48.693 --> 01:11:49.920
maybe I'm in the most boring part of it,

01:11:49.920 --> 01:11:51.347
but I'm still recommending it.

01:11:51.347 --> 01:11:52.437
"Get back."

01:11:53.800 --> 01:11:55.100
All right. Speaking of that,

01:11:55.100 --> 01:11:57.883
we will get back with you next week.

01:11:58.830 --> 01:12:01.570
Where we're gonna talk about our purchases

01:12:01.570 --> 01:12:03.800
from 2021 that we did.

